[{"file":"2026-10-29_personal-installation.md","title":"Personal installation instead of a per-project one","summary":"Let one person install OpenAgent for themselves, without adding it to a project's repository. The requester wants to use some of OA's skills on Vike (for example, account rotation) without pushing OA onto the project's other contributors. Today OA installs per project, so its skills and files get committed where every contributor sees them. Ideas are open: the issue asks for them.","topics":["install","skills"],"issue":{"label":"#2239","url":"https://github.com/openagt/openagent/issues/2239"},"date":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z","planned":false},{"file":"2026-10-26_dashboard-on-tailnet-address.md","title":"Dashboard on a tailnet address (Tailscale Serve / Funnel)","summary":"A dashboard behind a TLS-terminating reverse proxy on a non-loopback hostname doesn't work. Behind Tailscale Serve (`tailscale serve --bg 4200`, at `https://<host>.<tailnet>.ts.net`) the page loads, but every `/_rpc` call gets `403 unexpected Host header`. The cause is `isExpectedHost()` in `dashboard/rpc-serve.js`: it accepts only loopback hosts, and no setting changes that. The UI then shows \"The daemon is not answering\". Tailscale Funnel hits the same Host check. Its door also can't get its own Let's Encrypt certificate, because Funnel exposes only 443/8443/10000 and not port 80.","topics":["dashboard","remote-access"],"issue":{"label":"#2217","url":"https://github.com/openagt/openagent/issues/2217"},"date":"2026-10-26T00:00:00.000Z","planned":false},{"file":"2026-10-18_base-ui-rename-warnings.md","title":"base-ui rename warnings at install","summary":"Installing the dashboard from npm prints two \"deprecated\" warnings: `@base-ui-components/react` and `@base-ui-components/utils` were renamed to `@base-ui/react` and `@base-ui/utils`. We pin `@base-ui-components/react@1.0.0-rc.0` in three packages (`openagent`, `files`, `changes`), imported by 17 source files. Move to `@base-ui/react`.","topics":["dependencies","dashboard"],"issue":{"label":"#2143","url":"https://github.com/openagt/openagent/issues/2143"},"date":"2026-10-18T00:00:00.000Z","planned":true,"locked":true,"lockedBy":"2026-10-18T13-54-47-519Z","effort":2,"uncertainty":1},{"file":"2026-10-18_people-on-shared-computer.md","title":"People on a shared computer: each person's own runs, logins and laptops","summary":"A computer several people use (a server, or a computer at home several people start agents on from their own laptops) gives each person their own runs, logins and laptops' lines. A person is their GitHub account; a run uses the GitHub and Claude logins of whoever started it; each person keeps their own copy of a project there. Others' runs reach a person through GitHub (`agent-data`), read only. Only the computer's owner invites. Whoever connects a computer to a shared one picks who may use it: only them, or everyone there. A computer only one person uses is unchanged: OpenAgent asks who yogithub.com
